  "customHelp": "Manual Grand Quest table. Use the rules version agreed with your opponent.\nCaptain and Destination each have a home zone. Battleground 1-5 are five visual slots; players enforce occupancy.\nCrystals are individual cards in the Crystal Deck and Crystal Keep. The Aether tracker is a separate numerical pool.\nDraw your opening hand and perform any mulligan manually. Turn draws, refreshes, resource gains, payments and effect resolution are manual.\nTo ramp, move/draw a Crystal into the Crystal Keep and reveal it if it remains face down. Rest or ready the individual Crystal as required.\nResolve recruitment and combat response windows with your opponent. No attack legality, timing, damage, treasure awards or win conditions are automated.\nUse Wayside for discarded/destroyed cards. Keep attached Equipment grouped with its card where appropriate.\nChanging turns does not draw cards or ready rested cards in this configuration. Adjust Treasure and Aether yourself.\nCompatibility: Adventurer is the internal Captain category; Aether_Deck is the internal Crystal Deck category. These keys retain your existing deck format. Rename them only together with the card/deck data.\nKeep ongoing effects in Camp and group Equipment with its attached card. The zero automatic opening draw and zero tracker defaults are manual-table settings, not prescribed game rules.",
  "cardRotation": 45,
  "cards": {
    "dataUrl": "https://juun-llana.github.io/grand-quest-card-images/CardList.json",
    "cardBack": "https://juun-llana.github.io/grand-quest-card-images/Quest Back.png"
  },
